    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/45/5/thumb_19852.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 40125,
    "bookid": 45,
    "chapterId": 5,
    "fileId": 22092,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Astrocytoma, IDH-mutant, CNS WHO grade&nbsp;2",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "This unsuspected tumour was identified at autopsy in a man in his thirties who had last been known to be alive 2&nbsp;days prior; he was found dead at home. Note the exophytic right parieto-occipital mass lesion that blurs cortical anatomical features and is associated with cerebral oedema. Herniation was identified at autopsy and histological examination proved IDH-mutant status.",
    "source": "Bette K. Kleinschmidt-DeMasters",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/45/5/22092.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/45/5/thumb_22092.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 40126,
    "bookid": 45,
    "chapterId": 5,
    "fileId": 22093,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Astrocytoma, IDH-mutant, CNS WHO grade&nbsp;2",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "This unsuspected tumour was identified at autopsy in a man in his thirties who had last been known to be alive 2 days prior; he was found dead at home. Coronal sectioning of the brain (after brief formalin fixation) revealed a non-necrotic, ill-defined gelatinous tumour in the right parieto-occipital lobe, with mass effect. Note the ventricular compression and blurring of the grey matter&ndash;white matter junction produced by the tumour compared with the normal left side of the brain.",
    "source": "Bette K. Kleinschmidt-DeMasters",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/45/5/22093.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/45/5/thumb_22093.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 40294,
    "bookid": 45,
    "chapterId": 5,
    "fileId": 20218,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Grading criteria for astrocytoma, IDH-mutant</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "L.Peferoen - adapted from text submitted",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.45pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"179\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Grade</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 316.65pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"422\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Criteria</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"179\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>CNS WHO grade&nbsp;2</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 316.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"422\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>A diffusely infiltrative astrocytic glioma with an <em>IDH1</em> or <em>IDH2</em> mutation that is well differentiated and lacks histological features of anaplasia</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Mitotic activity is not detected or very low</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Microvascular proliferation, necrosis, and homozygous deletions of <em>CDKN2A</em>&nbsp;and/or <em>CDKN2B</em> are absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"179\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>CNS WHO grade&nbsp;3</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 316.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"422\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>A diffusely infiltrative astrocytic glioma with an <em>IDH1</em> or <em>IDH2</em> mutation that exhibits focal or dispersed anaplasia and displays significant mitotic activity</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Microvascular proliferation, necrosis, and homozygous deletions of <em>CDKN2A</em>&nbsp;and/or <em>CDKN2B</em> are absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.45pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"179\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>CNS WHO grade&nbsp;4</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 316.65pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"422\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>A diffusely infiltrative astrocytic glioma with an <em>IDH1</em> or <em>IDH2</em> mutation that exhibits microvascular proliferation or necrosis or homozygous deletion of <em>CDKN2A</em>&nbsp;and/or <em>CDKN2B</em>, or any combination of these features</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
